{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q8pKmTdKm1gD6yRpeCGcTD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan literals at land, test aim line, spacing rule\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\tLand refuses a task whose `Data:` names a backticked string found nowhere in its change or the tree, the build prompt tells each builder to test the exact case it claims, and the code rules fail on uneven spacing around `=` and a missing space after a comma.\n5\t\n6\t## Decisions\n7\t1. Scope is step 5 of the order in `.exo/advice/review.md`: section #5, Aanpak items 2-4; no citation rule (item 1), no ACC check (item 3 waits for ACC to recur), no CANTFAIL analysis (item 5). Closed by you.\n8\t2. A backticked `Data:` string passes when, after dropping a `:<line>` or `:<start>-<end>` suffix, it is a tracked file's path or basename; or it occurs in `git diff HEAD` or anywhere in the working tree, untracked files included; or, after dropping `<...>` placeholders and `...` and splitting on whitespace and punctuation other than `. / - _`, each fragment of 3 or more characters occurs there. Closed by exo: a dry run over 86 landed tasks (`.exo/land-literals/audit.md`) refused 26 tasks under the bare rule, all falsely, and 1 under this one.\n9\t3. The escape is a task field `Literals: none (<reason>)`, parsed like `Red:`; a task carrying it skips the check. Closed by exo, per section #5 Aanpak 2.\n10\t4. The spacing rule is an own line check in `lib/code-rules.mjs`, failing land, because the eslint path runs only when the project has `node_modules/.bin/eslint` (`lib/code-rules.mjs:157-158`) and this repo has none; it reads only code on added lines, with strings, template text, regex literals and comments removed, and flags ` =x` or `x= ` (but not `==`, `=>`, `<=`, `>=`, `!=`) as `space-infix-ops` and a comma followed by a non-space as `comma-spacing`. Closed by exo.\n11\t5. The test-aim line goes in the `Build session` section of `skills/build/run-task-prompt.md`, which every detached builder gets (`skills/build/scripts/run-prompts.mjs:52`). Closed by exo.\n12\t6. One test pair for the literal check, because a false refusal stops a run; no other new test. Closed by exo.\n13\t\n14\t## Non-goals\n15\t- `agents/build-task.md`, the interactive builder's prompt.\n16\t- Changing the eslint rule list (`ESLINT_RULES` in `lib/code-rules.mjs`).\n17\t- Literal checks in `plan-check` before a run.\n18\t\n19\t## Assumptions\n20\t- code: `skills/build/scripts/land-task.mjs:486-491` `refuseUntestedTestFirst(task, root)` throws `LandingError`; `:552` in `landTask` is its only call; `:625-635` prints `land-task: <message>` and exits 1.\n21\t- code: at `land-task.mjs:552` the task's changes are not staged; `taskChangedPaths` (`:445-453`) reads `git status --porcelain`, untracked files included.\n22\t- code: `lib/plan-tasks.mjs:132-143` `fieldSegments` splits task fields; `Data:` stays a raw string in `fields.Data`; `:74-76` `redOf` turns `none (<reason>)` into `{ reason }`, else null; `:203` sets `red`.\n23\t- code: `skills/spec/references/task-list.md:25` holds the task field template with `[ | Red: none (<reason>)]`.\n24\t- code: `lib/code-rules.mjs:97` `structureFindings(text, added)` runs line checks without eslint; `:11` `FAIL_RULES`; `:189` `codeOnlyLines`; `:222` `codeRuleFindings({ root, base, paths })` returns `{ fails, warns }`.\n25\t- code: `tests/land-task-fixture.mjs:104` `assertRefused(root, planPath, extraArgs, stderrPattern)`; `tests/land-task-commit.test.mjs` holds the test-first refusal tests.\n26\t- code: the two spacing findings were `noRedProofLine =(output)`, `taskSubject =(heading)`, `DEFAULT_LAND_GATE ='npm run check'` and a missing space after a comma, all in `.mjs` files (`.exo/kept/audit-run-records/branch-review.md:32,34`, `.exo/kept/efficient-loop/branch-review.md:68,70`).\n27\t\n28\t## Acceptance\n29\tSeam: `land-task.mjs` on a fixture repo, and `codeRuleFindings` on a temp repo.\n30\t- A parsed task carries its `Data:` text and its `Literals:` escape (Task 1).\n31\t- Land refuses a task whose `Data:` string is missing and names the string and the escape (Task 2).\n32\t- Land passes a string that is present, a file path or basename, or a placeholder form, and skips the check under `Literals: none (<reason>)` (Task 2 `Data:`).\n33\t- `codeRuleFindings` fails ` =(`, `='` and `a,b` in code, and passes them inside a string (Task 3).\n34\t- Each detached builder's prompt says a test observes the exact case it claims (Task 4).\n35\t- `npm run check` ends `FAIL=0 WARN=0 UNRUN=0` (Success criterion).\n36\t\n37\t## Manual checks\n38\t- The next real run lands its tasks with no `Data:` literal refusal it did not earn.\n39\t\n40\t## Plan basis\n41\tRepository: /Users/<user>/Documents/Code/personal/plugins/exo\n42\tBranch: land-literals\n43\tWorktree setup: none\n44\tLand gate: npm run validate:static\n45\tLand: local\n46\tCommit: feat(build): check plan literals at land and spacing in the code rules\n47\tLint: none\n48\tAllow: none\n49\t\n50\t## Success criterion\n51\t`npm run check`\n52\tRed: none (each task's Proof proves its own red)\n53\tProduct run: none (land-task and the code rules run inside a paid run; Tasks 2 and 3 drive them on fixtures)\n54\t\n55\t## Checkpoint\n56\t- Blocks first: none.\n57\t- Parallel: Tasks 1, 3 and 5.\n58\t- Shared state: `verify/budgets.mjs`, `verify/checks/reference-tables.mjs` and `CONTRIBUTING.md`, so Task 4 follows Task 1.\n59\t- Smallest safe split: the parser first, then one task per check, one for the prompt line, one for the changelog line.\n60\t\n61\t## Tasks\n62\t### Task 1: feat(plan): parse a task's Data text and its Literals escape\n63\tDepends on: none | Files: `lib/plan-tasks.mjs`, `skills/spec/references/task-list.md`, `verify/budgets.mjs`, `verify/checks/reference-tables.mjs`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Data: each task `parsePlan` returns gains `data` (its raw `Data:` text, else null) and `literals` (`redOf` of a `Literals:` field); `task-list.md` 