ort { join } from 'node:path'; import { codeRuleFindings } from './lib/code-rules.mjs'; const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'spacing-')); const git = (...args) => run('git', ['-C', dir, '-c', 'user.email=t@t', '-c', 'user.name=t', ...args]); git('init', '-q'); writeFileSync(join(dir, 'a.mjs'), 'export const a = 1;\\n'); git('add', '.'); git('commit', '-qm', 'base'); writeFileSync(join(dir, 'a.mjs'), 'export const a = 1;\\nexport const b =(a);\\nexport const c = [a,a];\\nexport const d = \\\"x,y =z\\\";\\n'); const found = JSON.stringify(codeRuleFindings({ root: dir, base: 'HEAD', paths: ['a.mjs'] }).fails).match(/space-infix-ops|comma-spacing/g) ?? []; if (found.length !== 2) process.exit(1)\"\n68\t### Task 4: feat(build): tell each builder to test the exact case it claims\n69\tDepends on: 1 | Files: `skills/build/run-task-prompt.md`, `verify/budgets.mjs`, `verify/checks/reference-tables.mjs`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Data: one `- ` line in the `Build session` section: a test the task adds observes the exact case its Acceptance item, `Data:` clause or changed branch names, not a nearby case | Proof: grep -qF 'observes the exact case' skills/build/run-task-prompt.md\n70\t### Task 5: docs(changelog): record the land literal check and the spacing rule\n71\tDepends on: none | Files: `CHANGELOG.md` | Data: one `- ` bullet under `## Unreleased` `### Added`, holding the Proof's text | Proof: grep -qF 'Land refuses a task whose `Data:` names a backticked string found nowhere in its change or the tree, unless the task sets `Literals: none (<reason>)`; the code rules fail on uneven spacing around `=` and a missing space after a comma.' CHANGELOG.md\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0c698e7-e566-4a08-9a99-c2a2cd2a8b3a","uuid":"365275f0-5b17-40ab-bd89-74f5ae5485c7","timestamp":"2026-10-16T21:43:08.264Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/<user>/Documents/Code/personal/plugins/exo/docs/specs/land-literals.md","content":"# Plan literals at land, test aim line, spacing rule\n\n## Goal\nLand refuses a task whose `Data:` names a backticked string found nowhere in its change or the tree, the build prompt tells each builder to test the exact case it claims, and the code rules fail on uneven spacing around `=` and a missing space after a comma.\n\n## Decisions\n1. Scope is step 5 of the order in `.exo/advice/review.md`: section #5, Aanpak items 2-4; no citation rule (item 1), no ACC check (item 3 waits for ACC to recur), no CANTFAIL analysis (item 5). Closed by you.\n2. A backticked `Data:` string passes when, after dropping a `:<line>` or `:<start>-<end>` suffix, it is a tracked file's path or basename; or it occurs in `git diff HEAD` or anywhere in the working tree, untracked files included; or, after dropping `<...>` placeholders and `...` and splitting on whitespace and punctuation other than `. / - _`, each fragment of 3 or more characters occurs there. Closed by exo: a dry run over 86 landed tasks (`.exo/land-literals/audit.md`) refused 26 tasks under the bare rule, all falsely, and 1 under this one.\n3. The escape is a task field `Literals: none (<reason>)`, parsed like `Red:`; a task carrying it skips the check. Closed by exo, per section #5 Aanpak 2.\n4. The spacing rule is an own line check in `lib/code-rules.mjs`, failing land, because the eslint path runs only when the project has `node_modules/.bin/eslint` (`lib/code-rules.mjs:157-158`) and this repo has none; it reads only code on added lines, with strings, template text, regex literals and comments removed, and flags ` =x` or `x= ` (but not `==`, `=>`, `<=`, `>=`, `!=`) as `space-infix-ops` and a comma followed by a non-space as `comma-spacing`. Closed by exo.\n5. The test-aim line goes in the `Build session` section of `skills/build/run-task-prompt.md`, which every detached builder gets (`skills/build/scripts/run-prompts.mjs:52`). Closed by exo.\n6. One test pair for the literal check, because a false refusal stops a run; no other new test. 