{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HD3DvPYZ1tGKHEB6DK5YSW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Review rules for fix findings\n2\t\n3\tBranch reviewer follows these when the dispatch names this file.\n4\t\n5\t## Dispatch\n6\t\n7\t- Pass: code standard path from `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md`, else `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/../route-skills/references/code-standard.md`.\n8\t- Pass: this file's path, plan path, branch, checkout, base, implementer report directory `<checkout>/.exo/`.\n9\t- Pass: scope `branch <base>..HEAD` from the one `REVIEW Branch` line, or `overlap` with the `OVERLAP` lines.\n10\t- Pass: findings path, named as input to `merge-reviews.mjs`: scope `branch` → `<checkout>/.exo/review-branch.md`; scope `overlap` → `<checkout>/.exo/review-overlap.md`.\n11\t- Scope `fix diff` → findings path `<checkout>/.exo/fix-review.md`, named as input to verify's repair step 3.\n12\t- Scope `fix diff` → `merge-reviews.mjs` never reads that file: it would overwrite `<checkout>/.exo/branch-review.md`.\n13\t- Scope `branch` → also pass three to five concrete questions, written from the plan's Goal and each task's `Data:`, `Risk:` and Acceptance line.\n14\t- Reviewer reads only the plan, diff and `Red:` lines: `.exo/proof-<plan id>-task-<n>.txt` first (plan id = plan file's name without `.md`), implementer reports when a task's proof file has none.\n15\t- Reviewer return with no file at its findings path, whatever its return line (`BLOCKED` and `CLEAN` included) → the dispatcher with SendMessage resumes it once, before any `BLOCKED` handling. If SendMessage is unavailable, dispatch a fresh agent with the prior result path.\n16\t- Resume message → names the path as input to `merge-reviews.mjs` (scope `fix diff`: to verify's repair step 3).\n17\t- File still missing, scope `branch` or `overlap` → pass that path to `merge-reviews.mjs` anyway, which merges it as `BLOCKED`.\n18\t- File still missing, scope `fix diff` → repair step 2 ends the turn.\n19\t- Merged `verdict=BLOCKED` → end the turn with its report, naming each findings path without a file; no second resume, no redispatch.\n20\t- Merge prints `UNREAD <n>` → list each unread finding in the `REPORT` file as `report`, name the count in the message; no fixer dispatch, no rerun, no rewriting the finding into one-line shape.\n21\t\n22\t## Probe\n23\t\n24\t- Each `fix` finding → line `  Probe: <command>` directly under it.\n25\t- Probe = one read-only shell command, run from the root, exiting non-zero now and zero once fixed.\n26\t- Run each probe once; keep it only if it exits non-zero; no such probe → mark the finding `report`.\n27\t\n28\t## Scope\n29\t\n30\t- Scope `fix diff` → diff is `git diff HEAD` plus files `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` lists, not base to HEAD.\n31\t- Scope `fix diff` → skip every task-by-task check.\n32\t- Scope `branch <base>..HEAD` → diff is `git diff <base>..HEAD`; read the whole plan; answer each question with evidence before the standard pass.\n33\t- Scope `overlap` → read each listed file and the named tasks' commits; report only a name, signature or reference two tasks disagree on.\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0c698e7-e566-4a08-9a99-c2a2cd2a8b3a","uuid":"4478eb4a-63d9-4392-8f2c-50803252a67e","timestamp":"2026-10-16T21:43:09.296Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/<user>/Documents/Code/personal/plugins/exo/skills/verify/references/review-rules.md","content":"# Review rules for fix findings\n\nBranch reviewer follows these when the dispatch names this file.\n\n## Dispatch\n\n- Pass: code standard path from `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md`, else `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/../route-skills/references/code-standard.md`.\n- Pass: this file's path, plan path, branch, checkout, base, implementer report directory `<checkout>/.exo/`.\n- Pass: scope `branch <base>..HEAD` from the one `REVIEW Branch` line, or `overlap` with the `OVERLAP` lines.\n- Pass: findings path, named as input to `merge-reviews.mjs`: scope `branch` → `<checkout>/.exo/review-branch.md`; scope `overlap` → `<checkout>/.exo/review-overlap.md`.\n- Scope `fix diff` → findings path `<checkout>/.exo/fix-review.md`, named as input to verify's repair step 3.\n- Scope `fix diff` → `merge-reviews.mjs` never reads that file: it would overwrite `<checkout>/.exo/branch-review.md`.\n- Scope `branch` → also pass three to five concrete questions, written from the plan's Goal and each task's `Data:`, `Risk:` and Acceptance line.\n- Reviewer reads only the plan, diff and `Red:` lines: `.exo/proof-<plan id>-task-<n>.txt` first (plan id = plan file's name without `.md`), implementer reports when a task's proof file has none.\n- Reviewer return with no file at its findings path, whatever its return line (`BLOCKED` and `CLEAN` included) → the dispatcher with SendMessage resumes it once, before any `BLOCKED` handling. If SendMessage is unavailable, dispatch a fresh agent with the prior result path.\n- Resume message → names the path as input to `merge-reviews.mjs` (scope `fix diff`: to verify's repair step 3).\n- File still missing, scope `branch` or `overlap` → pass that path to `merge-reviews.mjs` anyway, which merges it as `BLOCKED`.\n- File still missing, scope `fix diff` → repair step 2 ends the turn.\n- Merged `verdict=BLOCKED` → end the turn with its report, naming each findings path without a file; no second resume, no redispatch.\n- Merge prints `UNREAD <n>` → list each unread finding in the `REPORT` file as `report`, name the count in the message; no fixer dispatch, no rerun, no rewriting the finding into one-line shape.\n\n## Probe\n\n- Each `fix` finding → line `  Probe: <command>` directly under it.\n- Probe = one read-only shell command, run from the root, exiting non-zero now and zero once fixed.\n- Run each probe once; keep it only if it exits non-zero; no such probe → mark the finding `report`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Scope `fix diff` → diff is `git diff HEAD` plus files `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` lists, not base to HEAD.\n- Scope `fix diff` → skip every task-by-task check.\n- Scope `branch <base>..HEAD` → diff is `git diff <base>..HEAD`; read the whole plan; answer each question with evidence before the standard pass.\n- Scope `overlap` → read each listed file and the named tasks' commits; report only a name, signature or reference two tasks disagree on.\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HD3DvPYZ1tGKHEB6DK5YSW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
